code_review.final_verdict:
VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED

The entity change, schema updates across all four dialects, and the OpenAPI addition are all clean, additive, and idiomatic. The problem is placement of the defaulting logic.

**The "default registrationDate when null" logic belongs in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, not in the controller.**

`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:235) already owns exactly this kind of on-save field-massaging for owners:

```java
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.getTelephone() != null) {
        owner.setTelephone(normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone()));
    }
    if (owner.getEmail() != null) {
        owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
    }
    assertTelephoneUnique(owner, owner.getTelephone());
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

Setting a default registration date on save is the same category of concern — normalizing/defaulting owner fields at persistence time — and it should sit right next to the telephone/email handling. Concretely:

- **Wrong unit / split logic.** As written, owner-save invariants are now spread across two layers: some in the service, this one in the controller. A maintainer looking at `saveOwner` to understand what happens when an owner is persisted would not see the registration-date default, which is surprising.
- **Not reused across entry points.** The default only fires for callers that remember to set it. The service is the single chokepoint every save goes through (`saveOwner` is also called by the update path at OwnerRestControllerV1.java:128, and a V2 owner controller already exists at `rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`). Putting the default in the service guarantees consistent behavior regardless of the entry point, whereas the controller placement invites the same three-line `if (getRegistrationDate() == null) ...` block to be copy-pasted into any future create path.

Suggested change: remove the `if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) { owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now()); }` block (and the `LocalDate` import) from `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, and add the equivalent null-default inside `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` alongside the existing normalization steps.

